  "body": "Closes #1157\nClaim: mac/mac-mbp\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-w1157)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (mac/mac-mbp-r1236, mac/mac-mbp-r1236b: APPROVE on 1c10e0a6)\n\n**Problem.** Réglages › Taille du texte below 100 % scaled row text under the 11 pt HIG minimum (7.7 pt for `caption2` at 70 %).\n\n**Cause.** `TextScale.pointSize` multiplied the system size by the percentage with no floor. Legacy (`AppTextSizeScale.scaledUIFont`, `Common.swift:314-322` @ 87fe0d1c) never goes under 100 %, so it has no floor to port; the 70-130 % range is our own extension.\n\n**Change.** One place, `TextScale.pointSize` (every `scaledFont` and `font` goes through it): when the factor is below 1, the size is `max(system * factor, min(system, 11))`. 100 % and above are untouched; a size the system already gives under 11 pt (small Dynamic Type) is not raised. Legacy behaviour unchanged, so no ledger entry. The reader's web view scales through `factor` in a script, not this function: not changed here, tracked in #1237. The 11 pt hierarchy collapse at 70 % (subheadline, caption, caption2 all 11 pt) is an accepted consequence, recorded in the LOT-169 spec.\n\n**Tests** (`TextScaleTests`, iPhone 18 Pro simulator, iOS 27.2): `shrunkTextNeverGoesUnderElevenPoints` (15 issues) and `belowTheDefaultOnlyTheFloorChangesTheScaledSize` (2 issues) fail without the change, pass with it; `thePercentageMultipliesTheSystemSizeOfEveryStyle` adjusted for the floor; `seventyPercentIsSmallerThanTheDefault` skips styles already at 11 pt. `ListDensityLayoutTests`, `ReaderTextScaleTests`, `ComposerBarMetricsTests` green. No screenshots (a list needs a login; none typed). The device/list check at 70 % (Favoris, Messages, xSmall) goes to the next general review list on #893.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CFeNfBA416G5kNZLfw\n\n",
