   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, mac/mac-mbp-r1236b, head 1c10e0a6): APPROVE**\n\nAll five round-1 findings are fixed, for the whole class:\n- **R1 (reader):** follow-up #1237 is open; the PR body and the spec cite it. The reader scales through `factor` in `ReaderWebController+Scripts.swift:88`, outside this fix.\n- **R2 (docs):** `TextScale.swift:9-10,27` and the spec (`LOT-169:37-38`) describe the floor; the \"Topics 70 %\" row (`:48`) is marked outdated. A search of `App/` and `docs/` for text still saying the percentage multiplies every size finds one hit, `FormattingToolbar.swift:4`, which is still true (toolbar cell sizes go through `factor`, no floor).\n- **R3 (11 pt hierarchy):** recorded in the spec as an accepted consequence.\n- **R4 (`min(system, 11)`):** a why-comment says the branch is defensive.\n- **R5 (70 % check):** listed for #893.\n\nNotes, none blocking:\n1. **Low**, `TextScaleTests.swift:36-40`: the xSmall checks pass whether or not the `min(system, 11)` branch exists (no system style is under 11 pt); consistent with the \"defensive\" comment, but these lines do not test that branch.\n2. **Low**: `ListDensityLayoutTests.seventyPercentShowsMoreRowsThanTheDefault` comes from the author's simulator run; the 44 pt minimum row height probably keeps the 70 % row count unchanged. CI should confirm.\n\n**Checked:** the diff, the round-1 verdict and reply; every caller of `pointSize`, `scaled()` and `factor` (only text goes through the floor); the tests by reading (without the fix caption2 at 70 % is 7.7 pt, so `shrunkTextNeverGoesUnderElevenPoints` and the `== 11` checks fail; accessibility sizes still grow strictly, body at 70 % is 11.9 pt); line lengths (max 140). Not run: SwiftLint, the tests, the simulator; CI was still running on 1c10e0a6.\n\nAgent: mac/mac-mbp-r1236b (Opus 5.5)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
